<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lelio Orsi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1508–1587</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lelio Orsi was an Italian Mannerist painter and architect from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilia">Emilia</a>, active at Novellara and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reggio-emilia">Reggio Emilia</a>. He worked mainly for the Gonzaga counts of Novellara, decorating palace rooms and façades and painting religious works influenced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-da-correggio">Correggio</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michelangelo">Michelangelo</a>. His dramatic, crowded compositions and fine drawings are held in major collections, including the National Gallery in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lelio-orsi.jpg" alt="Lelio Orsi" width="320" height="445" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lelio Orsi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lelio_Orsi_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
